  "description": "Async pipeline runtime for .NET where pipelines compose: a compiled pipeline is a value, so one can sit in an object's context, ride in your task data, run as a step of another pipeline, or recurse and call other pipelines in a circle through PipelineRef, with no orchestration code around RunAsync. Also: resource-gated concurrency with adaptive/Bayesian tuning (and a pluggable custom-tuner hook, e.g. the always-learning EvalApp.Neural), sagas with compensation, middleware, exclusive-resource guards that fail loudly or queue when two flows touch something non-thread-safe, a single-thread host mode (detected automatically on Blazor WebAssembly, one-core or CPU-pinned processes) that runs inline and yields cooperatively so a UI stays responsive, and a fluent builder. One entry point, one namespace: using EvalApp; then Eval.App(...), and the whole public surface lives directly in the EvalApp namespace. The shared runtime for Evaluated Applications products.",
